ALTERNATE-VERTEX / INFORMATION AUDIT
==============================================================================
original tournament vertices: preserve local arcs/scores; destroy needle-boundary totals after quotient
arc-flip events/orbits: preserve one-step target incidence; destroy multi-step wall chronology
Hamiltonian needles: preserve H and the one-defect boundary U1; counts forget the failed-arc owner
path gaps/forward-count bins: preserve A_T and every averaged H mode; destroy target-W incidence
Walsh/Fourier modes: preserve all future means of H; destroy transition law already at n=5
Farey gaps (ordered denominator pairs): preserve the interval-core W-profile and mediant rewrite
fixed sections/boundaries/wall events/cover arcs: need offset+owner+side to preserve local coverage
residues: preserve modular incidence; destroy metric clearance and carry
matroid circuits: preserve dependence support; destroy coefficients, scale, and strict inequalities
proof obligations: preserve the comparison being optimized; they are observers, not runners/arcs
LRC predicate audit: none of the H/tournament quotients preserve loneliness
the Farey-pair quotient preserves only the special {1,...,k} interval-core violation predicate
and its measures; it does not preserve arbitrary-speed LRC loneliness

